itlin Bennett", "username": "KaitMarieox"}, "content": "LOL! Florida Democrats short-circuit and call the COPS on me after I ask if they're excited to have their first BLACK governor\ud83d\ude02", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 16920}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATodfLHC5", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 36, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8934189, "raw_content": "", "author": "wst4", "created": 1794339784440, "profile_picture": "K15ahGsDhQtO", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "UntakenUsername", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.scored.co", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATodfLHC5.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.scored.co/post/V3nSUjGsGQbZ.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [{"reference": "/scale/vmV9A7aXEpRPaPdI.jpeg", "width": 538, "content-type": "jpeg", "height": 768}], "blurhash": "UyM%J{NGbvWV_NbHs:oLyEaeWCbGW;jYX8kC", "full_resolution": [1541, 1080]}, "title": "Well that didn't take long you morons. ", "last_comment_created": 1794343097541, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 4, "score_up": 36, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATodeF585", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 56, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8933991, "raw_content": "**2026 MIDTERM ELECTIONS: VOTER ID vs. NO VOTER ID \u2014 LOOK AT THE RESULTS**\n\nI decided to compare the states that require voters to present identification at the polls with those that do not.\n\nAccording to the National Conference of State Legislatures (NCSL):\n\n- **14 states do not generally require an ID document at the polls.**\n- **36 states request or require an ID document**, whether photo or accepted non-photo identification.\n\nHere are the results from the November 3, 2026 midterm elections, using the November 7 race-call snapshot.\n\n**14 STATES WITHOUT A GENERAL DOCUMENTARY VOTER-ID REQUIREMENT**\n\nCalifornia, Hawaii, Illinois, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Minnesota, Nevada, New Jersey, New Mexico, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, and Vermont.\n\n**GOVERNOR RACES:**\n- Democrats: 12 wins\n- Republicans: 1 win\n\n**U.S. SENATE RACES:**\n- Democrats: 7 wins\n- Republicans: 0 wins\n\n**36 STATES WITH VOTER-ID REQUIREMENTS**\n\n**GOVERNOR RACES:**\n- Democrats: 11 wins\n- Republicans: 11 wins\n- 1 race pending\n\n**U.S. SENATE RACES:**\n- Democrats: 13 wins\n- Republicans: 13 wins\n- 2 races pending\n\n**WHAT DOES THIS TELL US?**\n\nAmong the races called in this snapshot, Democrats won nearly every governor and Senate contest held in states without documentary voter-ID requirements.\n\nIn states with voter-ID requirements, the called races were evenly divided between Democrats and Republicans.\n\nThat's an interesting difference worth examining.\n\n\n**Look at the numbers. Ask questions. And follow the evidence.**\n\nSources: National Conference of State Legislatures (voter-ID classifications), Associated Press (2026 election results).\n\nhttps://www.ncsl.org/elections-and-campaigns/voter-id\n\nhttps://www.ncsl.org/elections-and-campaigns/voter-verification-without-id-documents", "author": "GarySevenX", "created": 1794331243959, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "TrumpVoter1", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "The Democrats won in every Senate race that doesn't have Voter ID 7-0 ", "last_comment_created": 1794340988021, "content": "<p><strong>2026 MIDTERM ELECTIONS: VOTER ID vs. NO VOTER ID \u2014 LOOK AT THE RESULTS</strong></p>\n<p>I decided to compare the states that require voters to present identification at the polls with those that do not.</p>\n<p>According to the National Conference of State Legislatures (NCSL):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>14 states do not generally require an ID document at the polls.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>36 states request or require an ID document</strong>, whether photo or accepted non-photo identification.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Here are the results from the November 3, 2026 midterm elections, using the November 7 race-call snapshot.</p>\n<p><strong>14 STATES WITHOUT A GENERAL DOCUMENTARY VOTER-ID REQUIREMENT</strong></p>\n<p>California, Hawaii, Illinois, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Minnesota, Nevada, New Jersey, New Mexico, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, and Vermont.</p>\n<p><strong>GOVERNOR RACES:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Democrats: 12 wins</li>\n<li>Republicans: 1 win</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>U.S. SENATE RACES:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Democrats: 7 wins</li>\n<li>Republicans: 0 wins</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>36 STATES WITH VOTER-ID REQUIREMENTS</strong></p>\n<p><strong>GOVERNOR RACES:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Democrats: 11 wins</li>\n<li>Republicans: 11 wins</li>\n<li>1 race pending</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>U.S. SENATE RACES:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Democrats: 13 wins</li>\n<li>Republicans: 13 wins</li>\n<li>2 races pending</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>WHAT DOES THIS TELL US?</strong></p>\n<p>Among the races called in this snapshot, Democrats won nearly every governor and Senate contest held in states without documentary voter-ID requirements.</p>\n<p>In states with voter-ID requirements, the called races were evenly divided between Democrats and Republicans.</p>\n<p>That's an interesting difference worth examining.</p>\n<p><strong>Look at the numbers. Ask questions. And follow the evidence.</strong></p>\n<p>Sources: National Conference of State Legislatures (voter-ID classifications), Associated Press (2026 election results).</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.ncsl.org/elections-and-campaigns/voter-id\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.ncsl.org/elections-and-campaigns/voter-id</a></p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.ncsl.org/elections-and-campaigns/voter-verification-without-id-documents\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.ncsl.org/elections-and-campaigns/voter-verification-without-id-documents</a></p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 5, "score_up": 56, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "2120051329548886074", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATodfL04r", "is_twitter": true, "is_admin": false, "score": 45, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8934075, "raw_content": "", "author": "kek_saved_the_world", "created": 1794334648088, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "t-bone", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "twitter.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATodfL04r.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://twitter.com/MarioNawfal/status/2120051329548886074", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Mamdani's law on full display.  Despite the city having laws requiring permits for street prayers that are likely to disrupt city affairs, not